    "user": {
      "login": "othermaciej",
      "id": 978436,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjk3ODQzNg==",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/978436?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/othermaciej",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/othermaciej",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/othermaciej/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/othermaciej/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/othermaciej/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/othermaciej/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/othermaciej/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/othermaciej/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/othermaciej/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/othermaciej/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/othermaciej/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2016-06-15T19:04:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-15T19:04:34Z",
    "body": "I'm not sure a page-wide pragma is a good solution, since pages may contain video that comes from different sources (for example their own, an offsite embed from a third-party video provider, and an ad) which may not be equally equipped to handle inline playback.\n\n---\n\nBy the way, I notice an undertone of complaint/frustration that iPhone Safari is different in this regard. Our read of the spec was that it allows presenting all video as full screen by default, or at least doesn't disallow it.\n\nIt may be that Safari on iPhone is the only UA that made use of this provision (I don't actually know for sure), but there's nothing intrinsically UA-specific about it. And in an era of smaller phone screens, hardware that could better optimize fullscreen playback, and webpages that were not specifically mobile-optimized, it seemed like a pretty reasonable choice.\n\nNow that all those factors have changed, we don't think it's right to enforce fullscreen on iPhones. But for legacy reasons we're not sure we can just reverse the default instead of giving an opt-out. If anyone has a better suggestion for how to resolve this dilemma, we are open to suggestion.\n\n---\n\nThere's a possible alternative here: instead of just a legacy workaround, there could be a useful feature to have video play inline by default, full screen by default, or respect the UA's default setting. In many cases, it may still be useful for video to play full screen by default on a device with a smaller screen. Officially the only way to do this would be to have your play button call enterFullscreen() before play() (I guess only the first time, if the player supports popping back to inline?), which is somewhat awkward. But we weren't sure the genuine feature version of this had enough value, so we're proposing what is effectively just a legacy workaround instead.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
